Object.assign(USAGE_NOTES,{"convince":["使人相信某事，也可说服某人采取行动。",[["convince somebody that ...","使某人相信……"],["convince somebody to do something","说服某人做……"]],"The evidence convinced the committee that the result was reliable.","convince 强调让人信服；persuade 常突出促成行动，两者有重叠。"],"persuade":["通过理由或劝说让人接受观点或做出行动。",[["persuade somebody to do something","劝说某人做……"],["persuade somebody of something","使某人确信某事"]],"We persuaded the team to repeat the measurement.","不能把 persuade to do 省略宾语直接用于“劝某人”。"],"accuse":["指控某人做了不当或违法之事。",[["accuse somebody of something","指控某人……"],["be accused of doing something","被指控做……"]],"The official was accused of hiding information.","accuse 用 of；charge somebody with 强调正式指控。"],"blame":["把错误或不良结果归咎于某人或某事。",[["blame somebody for something","因某事责怪某人"],["blame something on somebody","把某事归咎于某人"]],"We should not blame the operator for a design flaw.","blame somebody for 与 blame something on 的宾语位置不同。"],"deprive":["使某人失去本应拥有或需要的东西。",[["deprive somebody of something","剥夺某人的……"],["be deprived of sleep","睡眠不足"]],"The outage deprived researchers of valuable data.","deprive 的固定结构是 somebody of something。"],"provide":["供给资源、帮助或服务。",[["provide somebody with something","向某人提供……"],["provide something for somebody","为某人提供……"]],"The report provides readers with a clear overview.","provide with 和 provide for 结构不同；provide for 还可指供养或预先安排。"],"supply":["按需要或规定供给，常用于设备、物资。",[["supply somebody with something","向某人供应……"],["supply something to somebody","把某物供应给某人"]],"The vendor supplied the laboratory with new sensors.","supply to 常以物作宾语；supply somebody with 以接受者作宾语。"],"equip":["给人或设备配备必要工具、技能。",[["equip somebody with something","使某人具备……"],["be equipped to do something","具备做……的条件"]],"The course equips students with practical skills.","equip 不只是提供器材，也可引申为使人具备能力。"],"remind":["提醒某人记住某事，或让人想起另一事物。",[["remind somebody to do something","提醒某人做……"],["remind somebody of something","使某人想起……"]],"Please remind me to send the revised draft.","remind somebody about a meeting 与 remind somebody of a person 语义不同。"],"inform":["正式告知信息。",[["inform somebody of something","告知某人某事"],["inform somebody that ...","告知某人……"]],"We informed the participants of the schedule change.","inform 比 tell 更正式；不能写 inform to somebody。"],"warn":["警告可能出现的危险或后果。",[["warn somebody about something","警告某人注意……"],["warn somebody not to do something","告诫某人不要做……"]],"The manual warns users not to disconnect the power.","warn of/about 风险；warn against doing 表示告诫勿做。"],"assure":["向某人保证、使其放心。",[["assure somebody that ...","向某人保证……"],["assure somebody of something","使某人确信……"]],"I assure you that the files are backed up.","assure 后通常接人；ensure 强调确保结果；insure 指投保。"],"ensure":["采取措施保证某结果发生。",[["ensure that ...","确保……"],["ensure accuracy","确保准确性"]],"A second measurement helps ensure that the result is reproducible.","ensure + 结果／that 从句，不要与 assure somebody 混用。"],"insure":["为财产或风险购买保险。",[["insure a vehicle","为车辆投保"],["be insured against theft","投保盗窃险"]],"The equipment is insured against accidental damage.","在英式英语中 ensure 与 insure 通常区分明确。"],"expose":["使某物暴露于环境，也可揭露隐藏事实。",[["expose somebody to something","使某人接触／暴露于……"],["expose a flaw","揭示缺陷"]],"The experiment exposed the device to high temperatures.","be exposed to 是接触，不必然意味着受到伤害。"],"impose":["将规则、限制或负担施加于对象。",[["impose a restriction on something","对……施加限制"],["impose a tax on something","对……征税"]],"The protocol imposes strict limits on latency.","impose on 常见；不要写 impose somebody a restriction。"],"depend":["依赖条件、资源或人的支持。",[["depend on something","取决于……"],["depend on somebody for something","依靠某人提供……"]],"The resolution depends on the clock stability.","depend on 是常规搭配；depend from 在这一义项不自然。"],"rely":["依靠人、系统或证据来发挥作用。",[["rely on somebody","依赖某人"],["rely on evidence","依凭证据"]],"We cannot rely on a single measurement.","rely on 和 depend on 接近，rely 常突出信任／依靠的行为。"],"insist":["坚持观点、要求或行动。",[["insist on doing something","坚持做……"],["insist that ...","坚持认为／要求……"]],"She insisted on checking the raw data.","insist on + 名词／动名词；不是 insist to do。"],"suffer":["经历痛苦、损失或不利变化。",[["suffer from an illness","患有疾病"],["suffer a loss","遭受损失"]],"The project suffered a major delay.","suffer from 常指持续状况；suffer a loss 可直接带宾语。"],"belong":["属于某人或某类，不作一般进行时使用。",[["belong to somebody","属于某人"],["belong in a category","应归在某类别"]],"These observations belong to the same category.","通常不说 is belonging to；belong to 与 belong in 用法不同。"],"object":["表示反对；也可作名词表示对象或物品。",[["object to doing something","反对做……"],["raise an objection","提出异议"]],"Several reviewers objected to removing the control group.","object to 中的 to 是介词，后接动名词而非动词原形。"],"apologize":["因不当行为或麻烦向某人致歉。",[["apologize to somebody for something","因某事向某人道歉"],["apologize for being late","因迟到道歉"]],"I apologize for the delay in replying.","道歉对象用 to，原因用 for。"],"forgive":["原谅过失或伤害。",[["forgive somebody for something","原谅某人的某事"],["forgive a mistake","原谅错误"]],"Please forgive me for overlooking your message.","forgive 后直接接人，不能写 forgive to somebody。"],"participate":["参与某项活动、讨论或研究。",[["participate in a study","参加研究"],["participate in a discussion","参与讨论"]],"Twenty volunteers participated in the trial.","participate in；不说 participate to a meeting。"],"propose":["正式提出方案；也可表示建议采取行动。",[["propose a solution","提出解决方案"],["propose doing something","建议做……"]],"The authors propose a simpler calibration procedure.","propose 可用 propose that 从句；propose to do 有时表示自己打算做。"],"demand":["强烈要求；名词也可指需求量。",[["demand that ...","要求……"],["be in high demand","需求量很大"]],"The circumstances demand immediate action.","作为动词一般不写 demand somebody to do something。"],"request":["正式请求或索取。",[["request information","请求信息"],["request that ...","要求……"]],"We requested a copy of the original dataset.","request 通常直接接事物；request somebody to do 在某些正式用法可见，但 ask somebody to do 更自然。"],"require":["要求具备条件、进行行动。",[["require somebody to do something","要求某人做……"],["require approval","需要批准"]],"The procedure requires users to restart the device.","require doing 有“需要被做”的意义，如 the room requires cleaning。"],"enable":["使人或系统具备做某事的条件。",[["enable somebody to do something","使某人能够做……"],["enable access","启用访问权限"]],"The update enables users to export their progress.","enable somebody to do；不是 enable somebody doing。"],"allow":["允许行动，或使某结果成为可能。",[["allow somebody to do something","允许某人做……"],["allow for uncertainty","将不确定性考虑在内"]],"The new interface allows readers to switch themes.","allow for 是“考虑到／预留”，不同于 allow somebody to do。"],"urge":["强烈建议或敦促。",[["urge somebody to do something","敦促某人做……"],["urge caution","呼吁谨慎"]],"The reviewers urged us to clarify the assumptions.","urge someone to do 常用于较强烈的建议，不是中性的 suggest。"],"advise":["提出建议；可指正式专业建议。",[["advise somebody to do something","建议某人做……"],["advise against doing something","劝阻做……"]],"The technician advised us to replace the cable.","advise somebody to do；suggest 通常不用同一结构。"],"avoid":["有意避开、避免某事。",[["avoid doing something","避免做……"],["avoid confusion","避免混淆"]],"We should avoid drawing conclusions too early.","avoid 后常接名词或动名词，不能用 avoid to do。"],"consider":["仔细考虑；也可认为某事具有某性质。",[["consider doing something","考虑做……"],["consider something important","认为某事重要"]],"We are considering adding another control sample.","consider doing；consider somebody to be... 可以，但 consider to do 不自然。"],"deny":["否认某事、拒绝给予某物。",[["deny doing something","否认做过……"],["deny somebody access","拒绝某人访问"]],"She denied changing the data after submission.","deny doing 与 refuse to do 不同：前者否认已做之事，后者拒绝去做。"],"admit":["承认；也可表示允许进入。",[["admit doing something","承认做过……"],["admit somebody to a program","录取某人进入项目"]],"He admitted making a calculation error.","admit doing 通常表示承认已发生的行为；admit to doing 也可以。"],"resist":["抵制、反抗或避免屈从。",[["resist doing something","克制不做……"],["resist pressure","抵抗压力"]],"She resisted the temptation to simplify the results.","resist 后可接名词／动名词，不接 resist to do。"],"risk":["冒着发生不良结果的风险。",[["risk losing something","冒着失去……的风险"],["at risk of something","有……风险"]],"We risk introducing bias by excluding these cases.","risk doing；不是 risk to do。"],"afford":["有经济或条件上的能力承担。",[["cannot afford to do something","承担不起做某事的后果"],["afford an opportunity","提供机会"]],"We cannot afford to ignore these warnings.","afford to do 常用于负担能力，未必涉及金钱。"],"manage":["成功应付困难、达成事情；也可管理团队。",[["manage to do something","设法成功做成……"],["manage a project","管理项目"]],"We managed to recover the missing data.","manage to do 强调成功结果；try to do 不保证成功。"],"fail":["未成功；也可表示没有履行要求。",[["fail to do something","未能做……"],["fail a test","未通过测试"]],"The server failed to respond within the deadline.","fail to do 不一定表示主观过错，可只描述结果。"],"succeed":["成功完成目标。",[["succeed in doing something","成功做成……"],["succeed somebody","继任某人"]],"The team succeeded in reducing the delay.","succeed in + 动名词；succeed somebody 意为继任某人。"],"seem":["看来似乎如此，语气通常比直接断言弱。",[["seem to do something","似乎……"],["it seems that ...","看来……"]],"The two measurements seem to agree.","seem 是从现象得出的判断，不等于已经证明。"],"appear":["显现；或看起来具有某特征。",[["appear to do something","似乎……"],["appear in a journal","发表于期刊"]],"The signal appears to fluctuate over time.","appear 作“出现”是事件；作“似乎”是认识判断。"],"expect":["预计某事会发生，或认为应当如此。",[["expect somebody to do something","期望某人做……"],["be expected to do something","预计／被要求做……"]],"We expect the drift to increase with temperature.","expect 侧重预期；hope 表示愿望，未必预测会发生。"],"suppose":["假定；口语中也可表示委婉判断。",[["suppose that ...","假定……"],["be supposed to do something","本应／按规定做……"]],"Suppose the clock shifts by ten picoseconds.","be supposed to 往往表示规范或预期，不是一般的“猜想”。"],"appreciate":["欣赏、重视，也可表示理解某种处境。",[["appreciate your help","感谢你的帮助"],["appreciate the difficulty","理解困难之处"]],"I would appreciate it if you could review the draft.","避免 I am appreciate；appreciate 后直接接宾语。"],"congratulate":["祝贺某人取得成就或遇到喜事。",[["congratulate somebody on something","祝贺某人某事"],["congratulations on ...","祝贺……"]],"We congratulated her on the successful defense.","congratulate somebody on；不要与 celebrate something 的宾语结构混淆。"],"benefit":["利益／好处；作动词表示受益或使有益。",[["benefit from something","从……受益"],["benefit somebody","使某人受益"]],"Both groups benefited from the revised procedure.","benefit from 表示受益来源；benefit someone 表示受益者。"],"consequence":["某行为或事件的后果，不一定为负面。",[["as a consequence of ...","由于……"],["unintended consequences","意外后果"]],"As a consequence of the delay, we missed the deadline.","consequence 偏结果关系；consequently 是连接副词。"],"influence":["影响行为、判断或结果。",[["influence a decision","影响决定"],["have an influence on something","对……产生影响"]],"Temperature can influence the measured phase.","动词 influence 直接接宾语；名词 influence 常与 on 连用。"],"regard":["考虑、看待；名词形式可表示尊敬或方面。",[["regard somebody as something","把某人视为……"],["with regard to ...","关于……"]],"We regard this estimate as preliminary.","regard as 与 consider (something) (adjective) 的结构不同。"],"focus":["集中注意、讨论或资源。",[["focus on something","专注于……"],["a focus on quality","对质量的关注"]],"The discussion focused on systematic uncertainties.","focus on 为常用搭配；不是 focus to。"],"account":["解释、占比，也可表示账户或叙述。",[["account for an increase","解释增加的原因"],["account for 20%","占百分之二十"]],"These effects account for most of the observed variation.","account for 的“解释”和“占比”是两个不同的用法。"],"argue":["提出理由支持观点；也可争论。",[["argue that ...","论证／主张……"],["argue for a proposal","论证支持某提案"]],"The authors argue that the effect is statistically significant.","argue that 未必表示吵架；在学术英语中常表示有理由地提出观点。"],"acknowledge":["承认事实、局限，或正式致谢。",[["acknowledge a limitation","承认局限"],["acknowledge receipt","确认收到"]],"The authors acknowledge that the sample is small.","acknowledge 是承认并正视，不一定表示赞同。"],"address":["处理问题，或向某群体讲话。",[["address a concern","处理顾虑"],["address an audience","向听众讲话"]],"The revision addresses the main concern raised by reviewers.","address a problem 常指回应／处理，不保证问题已完全解决。"],"encounter":["意外遇到、碰上某种困难。",[["encounter a problem","遇到问题"],["encounter resistance","遭遇阻力"]],"We encountered a timing problem during integration.","encounter 直接接宾语；不要写 encounter with a problem（作动词时）。"],"overcome":["克服阻碍、困难或恐惧。",[["overcome an obstacle","克服障碍"],["overcome a difficulty","克服困难"]],"The team overcame several integration problems.","overcome 直接接困难；overcome by emotion 表示被某情绪压倒。"],"handle":["处理任务、信息或物体。",[["handle a request","处理请求"],["handle a situation","处理情况"]],"The new software handles errors more gracefully.","handle 与 solve 不同：处理问题不代表已经解决。"],"resolve":["解决冲突／问题；也可下定决心。",[["resolve an issue","解决问题"],["resolve to do something","决心做……"]],"The team resolved the synchronization issue.","resolve an issue 指结果；address an issue 只表示着手处理。"],"maintain":["维持状态；也可主张某观点。",[["maintain stability","保持稳定"],["maintain that ...","坚持认为……"]],"They maintain that the original assumption remains valid.","maintain that 是坚持观点，不是维护某个物理设备。"],"measure":["测量数量；也可作名词表示措施。",[["measure a difference","测量差异"],["take measures to ...","采取措施……"]],"We measured the drift at three temperatures.","a measure 可指“措施”，与动词 measure 的测量义区别。"],"challenge":["提出质疑，或构成难题。",[["challenge an assumption","质疑假设"],["pose a challenge","带来挑战"]],"The new data challenge the earlier interpretation.","challenge 不一定带敌意，在学术语境可表示有根据的质疑。"],"concern":["涉及、使担忧；名词表示关切、问题。",[["raise a concern","提出顾虑"],["be concerned about something","担心……"]],"The main concern is the stability of the reference clock.","concerned about 是担心；concerned with 可表示与……有关。"],"commit":["承诺投入；也可犯错误或罪行。",[["commit to doing something","承诺做……"],["commit an error","犯错误"]],"We committed to improving the documentation.","commit to 中的 to 是介词，后常接动名词。"],"concentrate":["集中精神或资源。",[["concentrate on something","集中于……"],["concentrate resources","集中资源"]],"Let us concentrate on the main source of uncertainty.","concentrate on 通常比 focus on 更强调注意力的集中。"],"compare":["比较对象，可能着重相同点和不同点。",[["compare A with B","将 A 与 B 进行比较"],["compare favorably with","相比之下表现良好"]],"We compared the observed rate with the expected rate.","不要机械地把 compare to 只理解为比喻；现代英语中两者有交叉。"],"contrast":["突出两者差异。",[["contrast A with B","把 A 和 B 作对比"],["in contrast to ...","与……相反"]],"The results contrast sharply with the earlier report.","contrast 常着重差异，compare 可同时关注相似和不同。"],"correspond":["相对应，或与人通信。",[["correspond to something","对应于……"],["correspond with somebody","与某人通信"]],"Each label corresponds to a unique detector element.","correspond to 表示对应；correspond with 可表示通信，也可表示相符。"],"adjust":["作小幅或有针对性的调整。",[["adjust a setting","调整设置"],["adjust for a factor","对某因素作调整"]],"We adjusted for temperature differences in the analysis.","adjust for 是统计上控制／校正因素，不等于调整某个物理参数。"],"compensate":["弥补损失、偏差或付出的劳动。",[["compensate for a loss","弥补损失"],["compensate somebody for something","就某事补偿某人"]],"The correction compensates for the observed drift.","compensate for 是补偿效应；compensate somebody for 指给予补偿。"],"correct":["修正错误；形容词表示正确。",[["correct an error","修正错误"],["correct for a bias","对偏差进行校正"]],"The analysis corrects for detector inefficiency.","correct for 在数据分析中常指应用校正，而非简单“说法正确”。"]});
Object.assign(SENSE_FOCUS,{"bear":[["v.","to carry or support a weight or responsibility","承担；承载","The structure can bear a heavy load."],["v.","to tolerate something unpleasant","忍受","I cannot bear the noise."],["v.","to produce or give rise to something","产生；结出","After months of work, the effort finally bore fruit."]],"draft":[["n.","an early version of a text","草稿","Please review the first draft."],["v.","to write an initial version","起草","She drafted the agreement."],["n.","a flow of air through a room","穿堂风；气流","There is a cold draft near the window."]],"engage":[["v.","to take part in an activity","参与","Students engage in discussion."],["v.","to attract and hold attention","吸引注意","The lecture engaged the audience."],["v.","to hire someone for a purpose","聘请","The firm engaged a consultant."]],"credit":[["n.","recognition for an achievement","功劳；赞誉","She deserves credit for the design."],["n.","an arrangement allowing delayed payment","信用；信贷","The purchase was made on credit."],["v.","to attribute something to a cause or person","归功于","Researchers credited the improvement to calibration."]],"course":[["n.","a sequence of lessons or training","课程","She enrolled in a statistics course."],["n.","a direction or path followed","路线；发展方向","The project changed course."],["n.","a part of a meal","一道菜","Dessert was the final course."]],"point":[["n.","the central idea or purpose of a statement","要点","The point is that the sample is too small."],["n.","a particular position or moment","点；时刻","At this point, more evidence is needed."],["v.","to direct attention with a finger or indication","指向","The arrow points to the correct value."]],"regard":[["v.","to consider someone or something in a particular way","看待；认为","We regard the measurement as preliminary."],["n.","respect or admiration","尊敬","She is held in high regard."],["n.","a particular aspect or respect","方面","In this regard, the results agree."]],"fine":[["adj.","of high quality or acceptable","好的；不错的","The resolution is fine for this purpose."],["adj.","very small or delicate","细微的","A fine adjustment is necessary."],["n.","money paid as a penalty","罚款","The company paid a substantial fine."]],"current":[["adj.","happening or existing now","当前的","The current configuration is stable."],["n.","flow of electric charge","电流","The circuit draws a small current."],["n.","movement of water or air","水流；气流","A strong current pushed the boat downstream."]],"mark":[["v.","to indicate or label something","标记","Mark the outliers on the plot."],["n.","a visible trace or symbol","记号；痕迹","A mark appears on the surface."],["n.","a score given for academic work","分数","She received a high mark on the exam."]],"trace":[["v.","to follow or identify the path or origin of something","追踪；溯源","We traced the error to an incorrect setting."],["n.","a very small quantity","微量","Only a trace of contamination remained."],["n.","a line showing a signal or movement","轨迹；波形","The oscilloscope trace shows the rising edge."]]});

